            ]
          },
          "worked": "$1^2<3<2^2$, so start with $1<\\sqrt3<2$. At each step, square the midpoint and retain the half containing $\\sqrt3$.\n\n$1.5^2=2.25<3$, so $1.5<\\sqrt3<2$.\n\n$1.75^2=3.0625>3$, so $1.5<\\sqrt3<1.75$.\n\n$1.625^2=2.640625<3$, so $1.625<\\sqrt3<1.75$.\n\n$1.6875^2=2.84765625<3$, so $1.6875<\\sqrt3<1.75$.\n\n$1.71875^2=2.9541015625<3$, so $1.71875<\\sqrt3<1.75$.\n\nEvery number in this final interval rounds to $1.7$ to one decimal place. Therefore, $\\sqrt3\\approx1.7$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 108
