          },
          "worked": "$2^2<5<3^2$, so start with $2<\\sqrt5<3$. At each step, square the midpoint and retain the half containing $\\sqrt5$.\n\n$2.5^2=6.25>5$, so $2<\\sqrt5<2.5$.\n\n$2.25^2=5.0625>5$, so $2<\\sqrt5<2.25$.\n\n$2.125^2=4.515625<5$, so $2.125<\\sqrt5<2.25$.\n\n$2.1875^2=4.78515625<5$, so $2.1875<\\sqrt5<2.25$.\n\nEvery number in this final interval rounds to $2.2$ to one decimal place. Therefore, $\\sqrt5\\approx2.2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
