            ]
          },
          "worked": "$2^2<6<3^2$, so start with $2<\\sqrt6<3$. At each step, square the midpoint and retain the half containing $\\sqrt6$.\n\n$2.5^2>6$, so $2<\\sqrt6<2.5$.\n\n$2.25^2<6$, so $2.25<\\sqrt6<2.5$.\n\n$2.375^2<6$, so $2.375<\\sqrt6<2.5$.\n\n$2.4375^2<6$, so $2.4375<\\sqrt6<2.5$.\n\n$2.46875^2>6$, so $2.4375<\\sqrt6<2.46875$.\n\n$2.453125^2>6$, so $2.4375<\\sqrt6<2.453125$.\n\n$2.4453125^2<6$, so $2.4453125<\\sqrt6<2.453125$.\n\n$2.44921875^2<6$, so $2.44921875<\\sqrt6<2.453125$.\n\n$2.451171875^2>6$, so $2.44921875<\\sqrt6<2.451171875$.\n\n$2.4501953125^2>6$, so $2.44921875<\\sqrt6<2.4501953125$.\n\n$2.44970703125^2>6$, so $2.44921875<\\sqrt6<2.44970703125$.\n\nThe final interval lies between $2.35$ and $2.45$, so $\\sqrt6\\approx2.4$ to one decimal place.",
