          "worked": "$2^2<7<3^2$, so start with $2<\\sqrt7<3$. At each step, square the midpoint and retain the half containing $\\sqrt7$.\n\n$2.5^2=6.25<7$, so $2.5<\\sqrt7<3$.\n\n$2.75^2=7.5625>7$, so $2.5<\\sqrt7<2.75$.\n\n$2.625^2=6.890625<7$, so $2.625<\\sqrt7<2.75$.\n\n$2.6875^2=7.22265625>7$, so $2.625<\\sqrt7<2.6875$.\n\n$2.65625^2=7.0556640625>7$, so $2.625<\\sqrt7<2.65625$.\n\n$2.640625^2=6.972900390625<7$, so $2.640625<\\sqrt7<2.65625$.\n\n$2.6484375^2=7.01422119140625>7$, so $2.640625<\\sqrt7<2.6484375$.\n\nThe final interval lies between $2.55$ and $2.65$, so $\\sqrt7\\approx2.6$ to one decimal place.",
